    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance measurements. It assumes a cluster of N nodes, each running one or more serving processes (\"ranks\"), coordinated by a scheduler or orchestrator.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every rank is running the same logical system before any measurement is trusted.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files. Verify all ranks load from the same hash (or explicitly documented sharded equivalents). A rank serving a stale checkpoint is the most common silent failure.\n- [ ] **Engine/build version.** Capture the serving framework version, commit hash if built from source, and CUDA/ROCm driver versions per node. Diff across nodes; any mismatch is a finding.\n- [ ] **Parallelism topology.** Record tensor-parallel size (TP), pipeline-parallel size (PP), expert-parallel size (EP), and data-parallel replicas. Verify `TP \u00d7 PP \u00d7 EP \u00d7 DP` consistency with the actual number of GPUs allocated.\n- [ ] **Sampling parameter defaults.** Confirm temperature, top-p, top-k, max tokens, and stop conditions are identical across replicas. Divergent defaults make A/B comparisons meaningless.\n- [ ] **Quantization and dtype.** Verify weight dtype (FP16/BF16/INT8/FP8) and KV-cache dtype match the intended configuration on every rank. Log the actual dtype reported by the engine, not just the config file.\n- [ ] **Context window and limits.** Confirm max sequence length, max batch size, and max concurrent requests are uniform. A replica with a smaller context window will fail intermittently and only under",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
